{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2TI",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I charge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " therefore before God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, who will judge the living and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Preach the word; be instant in season, out of season; reprove, rebuke, exhort with all long-suffering and doctrine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the time will come, when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts will they multiply to themselves teachers, having itching ears;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they will turn away ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ears from the truth, and will be turned to fables.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But watch thou in all things, endure afflictions, do the work of an evangelist, make full proof of thy ministry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am now ready to be offered, and the time of my departure is at hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have fought a good fight, I have finished ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " course, I have kept the faith:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Henceforth there is laid up for me a crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will give me at that day: and not to me only, but to all them also that love his appearing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do thy diligence to come shortly to me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Demas hath forsaken me, having loved this present world, and hath departed to Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia, Titus to Dalmatia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Luke only is with me. Take Mark, and bring him with thee: for he is profitable to me for the ministry.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Tychicus have I sent to Ephesus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The cloke that I left at Troas with Carpus, when thou comest, bring ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the books, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " especially the parchments.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Alexander the copper-smith did me much evil: the Lord reward him according to his works:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of whom be thou aware also; for he hath greatly withstood our words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At my first answer no man stood with me, but all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forsook me: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I pray God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that it may not be laid to their charge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Notwithstanding, the Lord stood with me, and strengthened me; that by me the preaching might be fully known, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all the Gentiles might hear: and I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Lord will deliver me from every evil work, and will preserve ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his heavenly kingdom; to whom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Salute Prisca and Aquila, and the household of Onesiphorus.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Erastus abode at Corinth: but Trophimus I have left at Miletum sick.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do thy diligence to come before winter. Eubulus greeteth thee, and Pudens, and Linus, and Claudia, and all the brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2TI.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2TI.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The Lord Jesus Christ ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thy spirit. Grace ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with you. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
